* home-thermostat-3 project models. Sources and limits of every parameter: notes/models.md.
* Every subckt here is behavioral (written for this project) or a fit to datasheet numbers.

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- MAX17227A averaged boost
* ports: vin sw en vout gnd  (TDFN-8 pins 7 3 8 1 4; RSEL pin 6 is not modelled, RSEL 191 k -> 3.3 V, Table 1)
* Averaged, no ripple. Every number: notes/models.md and notes/datasheets/MAX17227A.md (data sheet 19-100743 Rev 1).
* - Input power = output power / efficiency, drawn at VIN (inductor DCR loss is inside EFF). EFFL at uA loads,
*   EFFH at mA loads, blended with the output current.
* - Input (inductor) current limit, average = IPK - ripple/2, ripple = VIN x tON(VIN) / L.
*   tON(VIN) = TONK x (86.7 ns + 640 ns.V / VIN): two-point fit through tON_1.2V 620 ns and tON_3.0V 300 ns (EC table).
* - ULPM offset: target = VOUT x (1 + OFS x w), w = 1 / (1 + (io / ITR)^4); ITR is the data sheet ULPM-to-LPM
*   transition current, ITR = eta VIN^2 tON^2 / (2 L 17 us (VOUT - VIN)) with eta 0.9 (Control Scheme section).
* - VIN >= VOUT target: the output follows VIN (synchronous-rectifier path). NOT stated by the data sheet (only
*   "VOUT > VIN + 150 mV while in regulation"): it is the upper bound of the rail (bench check, notes/models.md).
* - IQ into OUT (350 nA typ) and into IN (12 nA typ).
* VOUT, EFFH, EFFL, IQ, IPK, TONK, LIND (uH) and OFS are internal DC sources (Vref, Veffh, Veffl, Viq, Vipk, Vtonk,
* Vlind, Vofs) so that a corner analysis can change them with `alter @v.xu2.vref[dc] = ...`.
.subckt MAX17227A_AVG vin sw en vout gnd params: VOUT=3.3 EFFH=0.89 EFFL=0.90 IPK=2.0 TONK=1 LIND=1 OFS=0.027
+ IQ=350n IQIN=12n RREG=0.05 VUVLO=0.4 VEN=0.6 TAU=20u
Vref r1 gnd DC {VOUT}
Veffh effh gnd DC {EFFH}
Vipk ipk gnd DC {IPK}
Vtonk tonk gnd DC {TONK}
Vlind lind gnd DC {LIND}
Vofs ofs gnd DC {OFS}
Veffl effl gnd DC {EFFL}
Viq iq gnd DC {IQ}
Bon on gnd V = 0.25*(1+tanh((v(vin,gnd)-{VUVLO})/0.02))*(1+tanh((v(en,gnd)-{VEN})/0.02))
Bvx vinx gnd V = 0.5*(v(vin,gnd)+0.1+sqrt((v(vin,gnd)-0.1)^2+1e-6))
* on-time in ns
Bton ton gnd V = v(tonk,gnd)*(86.7+640/min(max(v(vinx,gnd),0.1),6))
* average input current limit (A), >= 0.1
Bila ila gnd V = v(ipk,gnd)-min(max(v(vinx,gnd),0.1),6)*min(max(v(ton,gnd),10),1e4)*1e-3/(2*v(lind,gnd))
Bilim ilim gnd V = 0.5*(v(ila,gnd)+0.1+sqrt((v(ila,gnd)-0.1)^2+1e-6))
* ULPM -> LPM transition current (A); VOUT - VIN smoothly limited to >= 20 mV
Bdv dv gnd V = 0.5*(v(r1,gnd)-v(vinx,gnd)+0.02+sqrt((v(r1,gnd)-v(vinx,gnd)-0.02)^2+1e-6))
Bitr itr gnd V = 0.9*min(max(v(vinx,gnd),0.1),6)^2*(min(max(v(ton,gnd),10),1e4)*1e-9)^2/(2*v(lind,gnd)*1e-6*17e-6*min(max(v(dv,gnd),0.02),10))
Bw w gnd V = 1/(1+min(max(v(io,gnd)/max(v(itr,gnd),1e-6),-100),100)^4)
Btg r1x gnd V = v(r1,gnd)*(1+v(ofs,gnd)*min(max(v(w,gnd),0),1))
Rref r1x r2 1k
Cref r2 gnd {TAU/1k}
* smooth max/min (no derivative kinks, so Newton converges): smax(a,b) = (a+b+sqrt((a-b)^2+e^2))/2
* target: follows VIN when VIN > target (assumption, see header)
Bvt vt gnd V = 0.5*(v(r2,gnd)+v(vin,gnd)+sqrt((v(r2,gnd)-v(vin,gnd))^2+1e-6))
* regulation current (A), >= 0
Bir ir gnd V = 0.5*((v(vt,gnd)-v(vout,gnd))/{RREG}+sqrt(((v(vt,gnd)-v(vout,gnd))/{RREG})^2+1e-12))
* output current allowed by the input current limit
Bim im gnd V = v(ilim,gnd)*v(vinx,gnd)*v(effh,gnd)/(0.5*(v(vout,gnd)+0.5+sqrt((v(vout,gnd)-0.5)^2+1e-4)))
* output current = smooth min(regulation, limit), gated by UVLO/EN
* review 2b: ir and im clamped to +-1e4 A before the smooth min (a non-converged Newton iterate gave
* 1e238^2 out of range in post-layout runs); no effect on any converged point (|ir|, |im| < 100 A)
Bio io gnd V = v(on,gnd)*0.5*(min(max(v(ir,gnd),-1e4),1e4)+min(max(v(im,gnd),-1e4),1e4)-sqrt((min(max(v(ir,gnd),-1e4),1e4)-min(max(v(im,gnd),-1e4),1e4))^2+1e-8))
Bout gnd vout I = v(io,gnd)
* io and vout are clamped to +-10 A / +-10 V inside Bin only so that a wild Newton iterate cannot overflow
Bin vin gnd I = min(max(v(vout,gnd),-10),10)*min(max(v(io,gnd),-10),10)/(v(vinx,gnd)*(v(effl,gnd)+(v(effh,gnd)-v(effl,gnd))*min(max(v(io,gnd),-10),10)/(abs(min(max(v(io,gnd),-10),10))+1m)))
Bq vout gnd I = v(iq,gnd)*0.5*(1+tanh((v(vout,gnd)-0.5)/0.05))
Bqin vin gnd I = {IQIN}*v(on,gnd)
Rsw sw gnd 100Meg
Ren en gnd 100Meg
Rvo vout gnd 1G
.ends MAX17227A_AVG

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- DRV8837 H-bridge, behavioral
* ports: vm out1 out2 gnd in2 in1 nsleep vcc (WSON-8 pins 1..8)
* Truth table (DRV8837 datasheet): nSLEEP=0 -> Z; IN1 IN2 = 00 coast (Z), 10 OUT1=H OUT2=L, 01 L H, 11 brake L L.
* RON per switch = 0.14 ohm (280 mOhm HS+LS). Input pull-downs 100 k. Sleep current IQS on VM.
.subckt DRV8837_BEH vm out1 out2 gnd in2 in1 nsleep vcc params: RON=0.14 IQS=0.1u
Rpd1 in1 gnd 100k
Rpd2 in2 gnd 100k
Rpds nsleep gnd 500k
Bh1 hi1 gnd V = 0.125*(1+tanh((v(in1,gnd)-0.5*v(vcc,gnd))/0.05))*(1-tanh((v(in2,gnd)-0.5*v(vcc,gnd))/0.05))*(1+tanh((v(nsleep,gnd)-0.5*v(vcc,gnd))/0.05))
Bl1 lo1 gnd V = 0.25*(1+tanh((v(in2,gnd)-0.5*v(vcc,gnd))/0.05))*(1+tanh((v(nsleep,gnd)-0.5*v(vcc,gnd))/0.05))
Bh2 hi2 gnd V = 0.125*(1+tanh((v(in2,gnd)-0.5*v(vcc,gnd))/0.05))*(1-tanh((v(in1,gnd)-0.5*v(vcc,gnd))/0.05))*(1+tanh((v(nsleep,gnd)-0.5*v(vcc,gnd))/0.05))
Bl2 lo2 gnd V = 0.25*(1+tanh((v(in1,gnd)-0.5*v(vcc,gnd))/0.05))*(1+tanh((v(nsleep,gnd)-0.5*v(vcc,gnd))/0.05))
Bsh1 vm out1 I = v(vm,out1)*(v(hi1,gnd)/{RON}+1n)
Bsl1 out1 gnd I = v(out1,gnd)*(v(lo1,gnd)/{RON}+1n)
Bsh2 vm out2 I = v(vm,out2)*(v(hi2,gnd)/{RON}+1n)
Bsl2 out2 gnd I = v(out2,gnd)*(v(lo2,gnd)/{RON}+1n)
Dh1 out1 vm DBODY
Dl1 gnd out1 DBODY
Dh2 out2 vm DBODY
Dl2 gnd out2 DBODY
Iq vm gnd {IQS}
* numerical aid: 1 Meg from each output to GND (about 3 nA at idle, added to the sleep load). The hi-Z coil nodes
* otherwise have only the 1 nS switch leak and the body diodes, and some MC runs failed at t = 10 ns. A capacitor here
* was tried and rejected: with the 30 mH coil it rings after the brake (coil peak 3.42 V, a model artefact).
Ro1 out1 gnd 1Meg
Ro2 out2 gnd 1Meg
.model DBODY D(IS=1e-12 N=1.1 RS=0.2)
.ends DRV8837_BEH

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- Panasonic ADW1103HLW, 1-coil latching
* ports: c13 c14 a1 a2. Coil: RCOIL (45 ohm -10 % = 40.5 ohm worst case for current and bridge drop).
* Contact state is not modelled (open, 1 Gohm).
* LCOIL 30 mH: ASSUMED (not published in a readable source), in series with the coil resistance. It sets the
* back-EMF energy 0.5 L I^2 that a coast at the end of a pulse returns to +3V3 through the bridge body diodes.
.subckt ADW1_1COIL c13 c14 a1 a2 params: RCOIL=40.5 LCOIL=30m
Rcoil a1 ac {RCOIL}
Lcoil ac a2 {LCOIL}
Rct c13 c14 1G
Rl13 c13 0 1T
Rl14 c14 0 1T
.ends ADW1_1COIL

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- ADS1115, load and input model
* ports: vdd gnd ain0 ain1 ain2 ain3 (VSSOP-10 pins 8 3 4 5 6 7)
* Supply 150 uA when VDD > 1.5 V; each input 6 Mohm common-mode impedance (FSR +-4.096 V) and ESD diodes
* to VDD and GND. The conversion itself (offset, INL) is applied in the measure expressions.
.subckt ADS1115_BEH vdd gnd ain0 ain1 ain2 ain3 params: IDD=150u RIN=6Meg
Bdd vdd gnd I = {IDD}*0.5*(1+tanh((v(vdd,gnd)-1.5)/0.05))
Rin0 ain0 gnd {RIN}
Rin1 ain1 gnd {RIN}
Rin2 ain2 gnd {RIN}
Rin3 ain3 gnd {RIN}
Du0 ain0 vdd DESD
Du1 ain1 vdd DESD
Du2 ain2 vdd DESD
Du3 ain3 vdd DESD
Dd0 gnd ain0 DESD
Dd1 gnd ain1 DESD
Dd2 gnd ain2 DESD
Dd3 gnd ain3 DESD
.model DESD D(IS=1e-15 N=1 RS=5)
.ends ADS1115_BEH

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- ESP32-C3-MINI-1 supply load
* ports: v3v3 gnd. Deep sleep (RTC timer + RTC memory) 5 uA + 32 kHz crystal oscillator 1 uA.
* Active currents (control wake, Wi-Fi TX) are testbench sources on +3V3.
.subckt ESP32C3_LOAD v3v3 gnd params: ISLEEP=6u
Bs v3v3 gnd I = {ISLEEP}*0.5*(1+tanh((v(v3v3,gnd)-1.0)/0.05))
.ends ESP32C3_LOAD

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- CJ2305 P-MOSFET (fit)
* Rds(on) 120 mOhm at Vgs = -1.8 V (search summary, unverified; round 3, replaces the 90 mOhm LCSC attribute):
* VTO -0.7 V, KP 8.26 -> 1/(8.26*1.1)+0.01 = 0.120 ohm; at Vgs -2.0 V 0.103 ohm.
* Body diode (round 3, R35 relies on it): IS 2.1e-13, N 1 -> Vf 0.75 V at 1 A, 0.455 V at 10 uA (25 C);
* 0.75 V at 1 A is the typical VSD of small SOT-23 P-MOSFETs (CJ2305 VSD not read, assumed). The former
* IS 1 nA gave Vf 0.24 V at 10 uA, unrealistically low. IDSS (<= 1 uA at -8 V, search summary) is not
* modelled by IS; see notes/models.md.
.model CJ2305 PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.7 KP=8.26 LAMBDA=0.01 RD=0.005 RS=0.005 IS=2.1e-13 CBD=150p CGSO=3e-6 CGDO=1e-6)

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- AO3413 P-MOSFET (fit, M1/M2 guard, M4 boost-input limiter)
* ports: d g s (SOT-23 pins 3 1 2). AOS AO3413 data sheet Rev 9.1 (Feb 2024), https://www.aosmd.com/res/datasheets/AO3413.pdf.
* Channel (level 1, W = L, no own junctions): RDS(on) typ 85 mOhm at VGS -1.8 V / 1 A, 70 at -2.5 V / 2.6 A, 56 at -4.5 V
* / 3 A (EC table; max 130 / 100 / 80). R = Rf + 1 / (KP (|VGS| - |VTO|)) with VTO -0.70 V (VGS(th) -0.65 typ at 250 uA;
* Fig. 2 transfer at VDS -5 V: 5 A at -1.45 V, 10 A at -1.75 V -> VT 0.72 V, KP 18.8): KP 23.6, Rf 46.4 mOhm (RD = RS 23.2).
* Model at 25 C: 85.8 / 70.6 / 57.4 mOhm; 79.5 mOhm at -1.97 V, 0.35 A (R4), 102 mOhm at -1.5 V, 1 A. Temperature: KP falls as T^-1.5 (level-1 default) and Rf has tc1 0.0037/K: about +8 %
* at 45 C (Fig. 4: 0.376 %/K, 1.0 at 25 C to 1.47 at 150 C). Level 1 over-states the saturation current at |VGS| < 2 V
* (Fig. 1: about 3 A at -1.5 V); the guard and the limiter run in the linear region (VDS < 0.2 V).
* Body diode (separate D, anode = drain): Fig. 6 at 25 C: 10 uA at 0.26 V, 1 mA at 0.38 V, 10 mA at 0.44 V (60 mV/decade,
* N 1.0): IS 4.0e-10. 125 C: 10 uA at 0.08 V, 10 mA at 0.31 V (N 1.0): IS(125 C) 9.7e-7 -> EG 0.71 eV with XTI 3 (fit,
* not the silicon 1.11 eV: the curve tempco is -1.8 mV/K). RS 0.07 ohm. Model at 25 C: 0.265 V at 10 uA, 0.38 V at 1 mA,
* 0.63 V at 1 A (EC VSD 0.7 V typ), 0.86 V at 4 A (Fig. 6 0.89 V); 0 / 45 C at 10 uA: 0.309 / 0.230 V; 125 C: 0.089 V. TT 9 ns (Qrr 27 nC at 3 A). Reverse: BV 21 V at 250 uA (BVDSS -20 V min); leakage = IS (data sheet IDSS
* max 1 uA at -20 V, 5 uA at 55 C, not modelled beyond IS).
* Capacitances (Fig. 8, EC at VDS -10 V: Ciss 560, Coss 80, Crss 70 pF): Cgs 490 pF, Cgd 150 pF (Crss at about -2 V,
* where the reverse-insertion step sits), body-diode CJO 50 pF (Coss - Crss at 0 V).
.subckt AO3413 d g s
Rd d di 0.0232 tc1=0.0037
Rs si s 0.0232 tc1=0.0037
M1 di g si si PCH_AO3413
Dbd d s DBD_AO3413
Cgs g s 490p
Cgd g d 150p
.model PCH_AO3413 PMOS(LEVEL=1 VTO=-0.70 KP=23.6 LAMBDA=0.01 IS=1e-30 CBD=0 CBS=0)
.model DBD_AO3413 D(IS=4.0e-10 N=1.0 RS=0.07 EG=0.71 XTI=3 CJO=50p VJ=0.7 M=0.5 TT=9n BV=21 IBV=250u)
.ends AO3413

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- CESD3V3D5 TVS (fit)
* ports: k a. Vrwm 3.3 V, IR 80 nA max (modelled as a 41 Mohm leak at 3.3 V), clamp 13 V at 16 A.
.subckt CESD3V3_TVS k a
D1 a k DTVS
Rleak k a 41Meg
.model DTVS D(IS=1e-12 N=1 BV=5.0 IBV=1m RS=0.5 CJO=15p)
.ends CESD3V3_TVS

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- 32.768 kHz crystal: DC stub
* ports: a b. The oscillator is not simulated; 1 Gohm leaks give the XTAL nodes a DC path (ESP32 pin leakage).
.subckt XTAL_DC a b
Ra a 0 1G
Rb b 0 1G
.ends XTAL_DC

* ---------------------------------------------------------------- MMBT3906 PNP (fit)
* JSCJ MMBT3906 (LCSC C2143). Typical-value fit: BF 200 (hFE 100-300 at 10 mA, datasheet range), IS 1.41f,
* VAF 18.7, BR 5; capacitances and transit times from the common 2N3906 Gummel-Poon set (same die class).
* ICBO: ISC 3 nA with NC 2 gives about 3 nA base-collector leakage under reverse bias (typical "few nA";
* datasheet maximum ICBO 50 nA at VCB -30 V, search summary, unverified).
.model MMBT3906_FIT PNP(IS=1.41f BF=200 NF=1 VAF=18.7 IKF=80m ISE=0 NE=1.5 BR=5 NR=1 ISC=3n NC=2
+ RE=0.5 RC=2.5 CJE=8.063p VJE=0.75 MJE=0.3677 CJC=9.728p VJC=0.75 MJC=0.5776 FC=0.5
+ TF=179.3p TR=33.42n XTB=1.5 XTI=3 EG=1.11)
